Kind: widen
Issue: #700
Holds open: a reply's window between taking its receiver off the queue and waking it -- 100 ms, while the receiver is being terminated, and that receiver comes back for its message 20 ms late so that the reply finds it still queued; each spin says so, so that a fixed arm that passes shows the window was open; in the fixed tree the spin runs under imq_lock, where the receiver waits for it; and thread_go() panics, its backtrace naming the waker, when it is about to wake a thread queued for the reaper
Run: --entry 14 600 -smp 4

diff --git a/uros/src/mach_kernel/ipc/ipc_mqueue.c b/uros/src/mach_kernel/ipc/ipc_mqueue.c
